# SMOKE AND FIRE DURING TAKE-OFF, take-off that cannot be aborted (format 1). The checklist is reproduced as printed in the DA50 C / RG Emergency Procedures checklist, Edition 4.1 of 2022-10-05 (owner decisions 2026-10-23 and 2026-10-27): the heading, the WARNING block, every item, action, comment row and sub-heading as printed. The row marks are the letters A to I of the AFM page that was compared. ASSUMPTION for the owner: the booklet may print numbers 1 to 9 instead; the marks are plain data (the `number` fields), so swapping them is one edit per row plus the typed table in tests/checklist-reference.ts. ECS shut-off PULL is the state pulled of the ECS shut-off; FUEL valve OFF is the state off of the FUEL selector; the Emergency windows row is graded on the emergency window and the Doors row on the door release lever, both optional because this simulation has no landing and the aircraft never stands still. The printed rows without a panel action (the short-cut circuit, the emergency landing with its reference and the evacuation) stay lines. All other text is own wording. The fire constants, the outcome threshold and hold time, the onset window and the forbidden items are copied from ENGINE FIRE in flight and are instructor-review values; the aircraft is airborne over the runway, so the speed holds at 70 knots and the runway keeps moving.
format: 1
id: takeoff-fire-no-abort
title: T/O FIRE NO ABORT
source:
  document: "DA50 C / RG Emergency Procedures checklist"
  issue: "Edition 4.1, 2022-10-05"
  section: AFM 03-32 IF TAKE-OFF CANNOT BE ABORTED
  verified: "2026-10-27"
disclaimer: training-aid
scene: takeoff_roll
briefing:
  situation: "You have just lifted off and are climbing out low over the runway at about 70 knots with flaps in take-off position. Smoke and flames come from the engine compartment. No message is shown on the primary flight display. There is no runway left to stop on."
initial:
  controls:
    lv.power: p100
    lv.flaps: to
    lv.gear: down
  quantities:
    fire_intensity: 40
    ground_speed_kt: 70
    airspeed_kt: 70
parameters:
  engine_fire: 1
annunciations[0]:
checklist:
  form: table
  heading: Smoke and Fire During Take-Off
procedure[12]:
  - kind: comment
    style: subheading
    text: If Take-Off CANNOT Be Aborted
  - kind: comment
    style: warning
    text: "IF, IN THE EVENT OF AN ENGINE PROBLEM OCCURRING DURING TAKE-OFF, THE TAKE-OFF CAN NO LONGER BE ABORTED AND A SAFE HEIGHT HAS NOT BEEN REACHED, THEN A STRAIGHT-AHEAD EMERGENCY LANDING SHOULD BE CARRIED OUT. DO NOT ATTEMPT TO TURN BACK TO THE AIRFIELD. TURNING BACK CAN BE FATAL. REFER TO 03-16 - ENGINE FAILURE DURING TAKE-OFF - EMERGENCY OPERATION PROCEDURE."
  - kind: group
    id: grp_ecs
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: ecs_pulled
        severity: critical
        number: A
        text: ECS shut-off
        action: PULL
        done:
          check: state
          control: lv.ecs_shutoff
          is: pulled
  - kind: line
    number: B
    text: If possible, fly along a short-cut traffic circuit and land on the airfield.
  - kind: comment
    style: subheading
    text: After Climbing to a Height From Which the Selected Landing Area Can Be Reached Safely
  - kind: group
    id: grp_shutdown
    ordered: false
    steps[3]:
      - id: engine_master_off
        severity: critical
        number: C
        text: ENGINE MASTER
        action: "OFF"
        done:
          check: state
          control: sw.engine_master
          is: off
      - id: fuel_valve_off
        severity: critical
        number: D
        text: FUEL valve
        action: "OFF"
        done:
          check: state
          control: sw.fuel_valve
          is: off
      - id: elect_master_off
        severity: critical
        number: E
        text: ELECT. MASTER
        action: "OFF"
        done:
          check: state
          control: sw.elect_master
          is: off
  - kind: group
    id: grp_windows
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: windows_open
        severity: optional
        number: F
        text: Emergency windows
        action: open if necessary
        done:
          check: state
          control: sw.emerg_window
          is: open
  - kind: line
    number: G
    text: Perform an emergency landing with engine off. Allow for increased landing distance due to the flap position.
  - kind: comment
    text: Refer to 03-41 - Emergency Landing with Engine Off - Emergency operation procedure.
  - kind: comment
    style: subheading
    text: When Airplane Has Stopped
  - kind: group
    id: grp_doors
    ordered: false
    steps[1]:
      - id: doors_open
        severity: optional
        number: H
        text: Doors
        action: open
        done:
          check: state
          control: lv.door_release
          is: open
  - kind: line
    number: I
    text: Airplane
    action: evacuate immediately
# The emergency fuel pump would feed the fire and fails the run. It is an instructor-review item.
forbidden[1]:
  - id: emerg_fuel_pump_on
    text: Switch on the emergency fuel pump
    fails_run: true
    trigger:
      check: state
      control: sw.emerg_fuel_pump
      is: "on"
# The outcome ends the run as a fail when the fire stays at a high intensity; the intensity and the hold time are instructor-review values.
outcomes[1]:
  - id: fire_spreads
    text: Fire spreads beyond the engine compartment
    hold_s: 20
    when:
      check: quantity
      quantity: fire_intensity
      op: gte
      value: 85
# The fire of the level Realistic begins at a random second inside this short window; the aircraft flies at 70 knots from the start (the PFD airspeed starts at the same speed). The window is an instructor-review value.
# The fire shows by its flames and smoke over the cowl, since the scenario lists no message; the lint checks that they show within seconds of the onset.
onset:
  window_s[2]: 2,6
  quantities:
    ground_speed_kt: 70
    airspeed_kt: 70
  cues[1]: flames
